WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.496
A context window is the amount of text, instructions, conversation history, retrieved content,

00:00:04.496 --> 00:00:08.216
examples, and tool output a model can consider during a request.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:12.613
It is the working space the model has available when producing an answer.

00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:15.995
Everything placed into that space competes for attention: system instructions,

00:00:15.995 --> 00:00:19.376
developer instructions, user requests, prior messages, documents, summaries, code, citations,

00:00:19.376 --> 00:00:22.420
and the output the model is expected to generate.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.787
Context is measured in tokens, not words.

00:00:24.787 --> 00:00:29.184
A token can be a whole word, part of a word, punctuation, spacing,

00:00:29.184 --> 00:00:31.889
or another text fragment depending on the tokenizer.

00:00:31.889 --> 00:00:36.285
The exact conversion varies, but the engineering point is simple: every instruction, document,

00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:39.329
example, and response consumes part of a finite budget.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:40.682
Output tokens matter too,

00:00:40.682 --> 00:00:44.740
because a request that fills the entire input space may leave too

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.769
little room for a useful answer.

00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:50.827
Large context windows change workflows because they let teams include more source

00:00:50.827 --> 00:00:52.518
material before asking for analysis.

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:56.238
A model can review longer documents, more code, richer chat history,

00:00:56.238 --> 00:00:58.267
or larger sets of retrieved evidence.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:03.340
That does not mean the model understands everything equally well or that structure stops mattering.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.722
More room helps only when the information is relevant, organized,

00:01:06.722 --> 00:01:08.751
and clearly tied to the task.

00:01:08.751 --> 00:01:10.780
Context management is an engineering discipline.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.176
It involves deciding what to include, what to summarize, how to order material,

00:01:15.176 --> 00:01:17.882
how to label sources, how to preserve provenance,

00:01:17.882 --> 00:01:20.925
and how to prevent noise from burying important facts.

00:01:20.925 --> 00:01:23.631
The goal is not to fill the window.

00:01:23.631 --> 00:01:27.689
The goal is to give the model the right information in a

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:29.380
form it can use effectively.
